The following files contain code derived from or modified from the original BitMEX project:
- market_maker/market_maker.py (heavily modified - main market maker logic)
- market_maker/__init__.py (modified - setup functionality)
- market_maker/settings.py (modified - settings loading system)  
- market_maker/_settings_base.py (extensively modified - adapted from BitMEX to TrueX)
- market_maker/utils/math.py (minimal changes - trading math utilities)
- market_maker/utils/constants.py (modified - trading constants and breakpoints)
- market_maker/utils/log.py (modified - logging utilities)
- market_maker/utils/errors.py (minimal changes - custom exceptions)
- market_maker/utils/dotdict.py (minimal changes - dictionary utilities)
- market_maker/utils/tick.py (modified - tick size calculations)
- market_maker/decimal128.py (minimal changes - decimal utilities)
- Makefile (modified - build and development tasks)

The following directories/files are entirely new and not present in the original:
- market_maker/external_data/ (complete directory - external data integration)
- market_maker/pricing/ (complete directory - advanced pricing models)  
- market_maker/local_data/truex.py (TrueX exchange integration, replaces BitMEX client)
- market_maker/order_adjustment.py (intelligent order adjustment system)
- scripts/run (unified launcher script)
- pyproject.toml (modern Python packaging)
- requirements-external.txt (external dependencies)
- All files in test/ directory (new test infrastructure)

Significant modifications have been made to the original work including:

CORE ARCHITECTURE CHANGES:
- Complete integration with TrueX exchange API instead of BitMEX
- Unified data provider architecture supporting both local and external data
- Modular pricing model system with manager and multiple strategies
- Reactive order adjustment engine separate from main market maker loop

NEW EXTERNAL DATA INTEGRATION:
- Abstract base classes for external data providers
- Coinbase REST and WebSocket data providers (no API keys required)
- Real-time market data fetching with fallback mechanisms
- Thread-safe data management and caching

ADVANCED PRICING MODELS:
- Simple spread model for basic external price tracking
- Consensus model for multi-provider price aggregation
- Local market-aware model combining external and local data
- Momentum-based pricing with volatility adjustments

ENHANCED ORDER MANAGEMENT:
- Intelligent order adjustment based on price movements
- Configurable adjustment thresholds and cooldown periods
- Batch order processing for efficiency
- Hysteresis prevention to avoid order oscillation

IMPROVED CONFIGURATION SYSTEM:
- Modular settings with base configuration and overrides
- Runtime mode detection (basic vs enhanced features)
- Environment-based configuration support
- Comprehensive logging and monitoring

DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW:
- Modern Python packaging with pyproject.toml
- Pre-commit hooks and code formatting (Black, isort)
- Makefile for development tasks
- Type hints and improved error handling

The resulting software maintains the core market-making logic while significantly 
expanding capabilities for modern trading infrastructure.
